+Production Proofs — Quick Guide
+
+This folder contains the orchestrator and test harnesses to run the production proofs required for Level 4 readiness.
+
+Steps:
+1) Configure prerequisites:
+   - Set EVIDENCE_BUCKET (S3) and ensure cluster service account has write access.
+   - Ensure Ray cluster and Tekton are available in the cluster.
+   - Place cosign key at /secrets/cosign.key on the runner or in a secure signer deployment.
+
+2) Apply Tekton PipelineRun:
+   - Edit ops/tekton/pipelineruns/production_proofs_pipelinerun.yaml to set your evidence bucket.
+   - kubectl apply -f ops/tekton/pipelineruns/production_proofs_pipelinerun.yaml
+
+3) Alternatively run orchestrator locally (requires network access and credentials):
+   - EVIDENCE_BUCKET=s3://your-bucket python3 ops/production/production_proofs_orchestrator.py
+
+4) After completion:
+   - Check acceptance summary uploaded under s3://<your-bucket>/production_proofs/summary-*.json
+   - If issues, run ops/validation/postmortem_generator.py with the summary JSON to generate action items.
+   - Iteratively remediate issues (drivers, OTEL instrumentation, policy tuning, remediation engine tuning).
+
+Notes:
+- Many steps are PoC and simplified; adapt monitoring/polling logic for production Ray/Tekton objects as needed.
+- For safety, Terraform apply remains manual & audited. Use terraform/scripts/manual_apply_and_audit.sh.
+
